<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Dinh dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">968 CE – 980 CE · capital Hoa Lu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The dynasty that reunited Vietnam after the anarchy of the Twelve Warlords and named the country Dai Co Viet, with its capital at Hoa Lu.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-tien-hoang">Dinh Bo Linh</a>, a local leader from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoa-lu">Hoa Lu</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ninh-binh-province">Ninh Binh</a>, defeated the rival warlords one by one and in 968 proclaimed himself emperor, Dinh Tien Hoang. He named the state <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/early-le-dynasty">Dai Co Viet</a> and built a fortified capital among the limestone hills at Hoa Lu.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-tien-hoang">Dinh Tien Hoang</a> ruled with harsh punishments to restore order, organised the army into units, and gave Buddhist monks official ranks. He sent tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>, which granted titles to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-lien">Dinh Lien</a> in the 970s, while using the title of emperor at home. Coins called Thai Binh were issued, among the first Vietnamese coinage.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 979 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-tien-hoang">Dinh Tien Hoang</a> and his eldest son were assassinated, leaving the child <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-phe-de">Dinh Phe De</a> on the throne. With a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> invasion looming, the commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Le Hoan</a> took power in 980 with the support of the queen mother, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/early-le-dynasty">Early Le dynasty</a>. Temples to the Dinh kings stand at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoa-lu">Hoa Lu</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dinh-dynasty.jpg" alt="Dinh dynasty" width="320" height="345"><figcaption>Image: Night Lantern · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vietnam_(1009-1225).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>968 CE – 980 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hoa Lu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dinh Tien Hoang, Dinh Phe De</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Vietnamese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Vietnam</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dai Co Viet, Đại Cồ Việt, Nhà Đinh</dd></dl></aside></div>
